      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: honor configured default agent across main paths",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes the remaining hardcoded `DEFAULT_AGENT_ID = \"main\"` assumptions called out in #90573 for deployments whose configured default agent is not `main`.\n\nPR #30654 fixed the main session-key write paths, but #90573 identified follow-on paths that still synthesized `agents/main/*`, `agent:main:*`, or phantom `main` audit scopes even when config declares a different default agent such as `nova`.\n\nThis PR uses the existing `agents.list[].default` / first-agent behavior. It intentionally does **not** add a new `agents.defaultAgentId` config key or `OPENCLAW_DEFAULT_AGENT_ID` environment variable.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe current behavior makes non-`main` default-agent deployments inconsistent: some surfaces honor the configured default agent, while others silently route storage, session keys, setup directories, or audit reporting through `main`. That creates broken paths and confusing phantom state for multi-agent installs.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDeployments whose configured default agent is not `main` can keep using their chosen default agent without residual `main` paths leaking into session initialization, auth/model storage scans, setup transcript directories, or exec-scope audit output.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Key new explicit `sessionId` sessions to the resolved store/default agent instead of literal `main`.\n- Thread the resolved agent id into auto-reply session initialization.\n- Resolve default auth/model storage scan paths from the configured default agent directory.\n- Stop security audit exec-scope reporting from injecting a phantom `main` default when another agent is configured as default.\n- Avoid inferring a delivery channel from one-segment agent main-session keys when the agent id happens to match a channel name.\n- Let setup create the configured default agent's transcript directory instead of `agents/main/sessions` when config is available.\n\n## Risk Mitigations\n\n- **Compatibility:** no schema/env surface added; legacy `main` aliases are still recognized where they already were.\n- **Auth-provider:** storage discovery still includes existing directories under state plus configured agent dirs; this only replaces the synthetic default path.\n- **Session-state:** new explicit sessions use the same effective default agent that owns the selected store; existing persisted keys are not migrated here.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/secrets/storage-scan.default-agent.test.ts src/agents/command/session.resolve-session-key.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/session-delivery.test.ts src/config/sessions/paths.default-agent.test.ts src/security/audit-exec-surface.test.ts`\n- `pnpm tsgo:core`\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check src/agents/command/session.resolve-session-key.test.ts src/agents/command/session.ts src/auto-reply/reply/get-reply-fast-path.ts src/auto-reply/reply/session-delivery.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/session-delivery.ts src/auto-reply/reply/session.ts src/commands/setup.ts src/config/sessions/paths.ts src/config/sessions/paths.default-agent.test.ts src/secrets/auth-store-paths.ts src/secrets/storage-scan.ts src/secrets/storage-scan.default-agent.test.ts src/security/audit-exec-surface.test.ts src/security/audit.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs src/agents/command/session.resolve-session-key.test.ts src/agents/command/session.ts src/auto-reply/reply/get-reply-fast-path.ts src/auto-reply/reply/session-delivery.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/session-delivery.ts src/auto-reply/reply/session.ts src/commands/setup.ts src/config/sessions/paths.ts src/config/sessions/paths.default-agent.test.ts src/secrets/auth-store-paths.ts src/secrets/storage-scan.ts src/secrets/storage-scan.default-agent.test.ts src/security/audit-exec-surface.test.ts src/security/audit.ts`\n- `git diff --check`\n- CI on current head `7896b83444`: all required code/security/check shards passed except `checks-node-compact-large-whole-1`, which failed in unrelated `ui/src/ui/terminal/terminal-panel.test.ts`; local focused rerun of that failing test passed: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.ui.config.ts ui/src/ui/terminal/terminal-panel.test.ts --reporter=verbose`.\n\nCloses #90573.\nSupersedes stale #17477 without adding the previously proposed config/env fallback surface.\n",
        "branch": "feat/configurable-default-agent-id",
